    "**Correct: B)** Hydropower is introduced right after the point about spreading sources across geography, as one more way to smooth supply: it \"can be stored behind a dam and released on demand.\" It functions as one ingredient in the diversified mix, which is option B. Option A promotes it to \"single best\", a ranking the passage never makes. Option C is a claim about rivers the passage never states. Option D is unsupported; hydropower is presented as a complement to solar and wind, not a criticism of them.",
