    "**Q23.** According to the passage, why is a national grid less vulnerable to intermittency than a single solar panel?",
    "A) A national grid uses only wind, never solar B) Rules guarantee a constant supply at all times C) Many spread sources make total failure unlikely D) National grids do not depend on weather at all",
