    "**Q27.** Which of the following situations best illustrates the passage's advice for building a new habit?",
    "A) Relying purely on motivation to exercise daily B) Linking new stretches to the cue of making morning coffee C) Punishing oneself severely for forgetting to floss D) Trying to break an old habit through sheer willpower",
    "<details><summary>Answer & explanation</summary>",
    "",
    "**Correct: B)** The passage's own example is doing push-ups right after brushing teeth, borrowing an existing cue's automaticity. Attaching stretching to the already-reliable cue of making morning coffee follows the identical logic, making option B the best match. Option A relies on motivation, which the passage never recommends and effectively argues against by favouring cues over effort. Option C is a punishment strategy, not a cue-based one. Option D is precisely the willpower-only approach the passage says fails.",
