    "**Q28.** The passage compares a habitual action to turning a doorknob mainly to suggest that",
    "A) habits require a great deal of physical dexterity B) the action needs almost no conscious mental effort C) habits always involve household objects D) doorknobs are a particularly common trigger for habits",
