    "**Q33.** The four sentences below, labelled 1 to 4, make a coherent paragraph when properly sequenced. Choose the correct order. 1. This single invention cut the cost of a book by a huge margin within just a few decades. 2. Before Gutenberg's press, every book had to be copied out by hand, a slow process that kept books rare and expensive. 3. Gutenberg's breakthrough was to cast reusable metal letters that could be arranged, inked, and pressed onto paper again and again. 4. Cheaper books meant wider literacy, which in turn fed the spread of new ideas across Europe.",
    "A) 2-3-1-4 B) 1-2-3-4 C) 2-1-3-4 D) 3-2-1-4",
    "<details><summary>Answer & explanation</summary>",
    "",
    "**Correct: A)** Sentence 2 must open, since it sets up the \"before\" problem: books were rare and expensive because copying was slow. Sentence 3 introduces \"Gutenberg's breakthrough\" as the solution to exactly that problem, so 2 must come before 3. Sentence 1 begins with the pronoun phrase \"This single invention\", which can only refer back to the press just described in sentence 3, so 3 must come before 1. Sentence 4 then continues the cause-and-effect chain from sentence 1's \"cut the cost of a book\" to \"cheaper books meant wider literacy\". The forced chain is 2-3-1-4. Option B ignores the pronoun anchor linking 3 and 1. Option C separates 2 from 3, breaking the problem-solution link. Option D opens with the invention before the problem it solves has even been introduced.",
