    "**Q34.** The four sentences below, labelled 1 to 4, make a coherent paragraph when properly sequenced. Choose the correct order. 1. Yemeni traders then carried coffee further, into the bustling ports of the Ottoman Empire. 2. Coffee was first cultivated in the highlands of Ethiopia, where legend says a goatherd noticed his goats grew energetic after eating certain red berries. 3. Within a century, coffeehouses had become a fixture of city life from Istanbul to Venice. 4. From there, the practice of brewing the berries into a drink travelled north across the Red Sea into Yemen.",
