    "**Correct: C)** Sentence 2 must open, as it is the only sentence describing an origin point (Ethiopia) rather than a movement from somewhere. Sentence 4 begins \"From there\", a phrase that needs the place named in sentence 2, so 2 must come before 4. Sentence 1 begins \"Yemeni traders\", picking up exactly the destination reached at the end of sentence 4 (Yemen), so 4 must come before 1. Sentence 3 concludes with a time marker, \"Within a century\", summarising the spread just completed in sentence 1 (the Ottoman ports), so it must close the paragraph. The forced order is 2-4-1-3. Option A breaks the \"From there\" link. Option B opens with traders arriving in the Ottoman Empire before Yemen has even been mentioned. Option D puts the concluding sentence before the traders have finished their journey.",
