    "**Q35.** The four sentences below, labelled 1 to 4, make a coherent paragraph when properly sequenced. Choose the correct order. 1. Choosing the right gear, then, is really a choice about how much wheel-turning each push of the pedal should buy. 2. A bicycle's pedals are connected to a large gear called the chainring, which turns a chain looped around a smaller gear at the rear wheel. 3. The opposite shift — a larger chainring paired with a smaller rear gear — turns the rear wheel more per stroke, favouring speed on flat ground. 4. When a rider shifts to a smaller chainring or a larger rear gear, each pedal stroke turns the rear wheel less, making climbing easier.",
