    "**Q36.** The four sentences below, labelled 1 to 4, make a coherent paragraph when properly sequenced. Choose the correct order. 1. Home refrigerators, once compressors became small and affordable, then replaced the icebox entirely by the mid-twentieth century. 2. Before mechanical refrigeration, families kept food cold using blocks of ice cut from frozen lakes each winter and stored in insulated ice houses. 3. The invention of mechanical compressors that could chill air on demand eventually made the seasonal ice harvest unnecessary. 4. This ice trade grew into a booming industry, with ships carrying frozen lake blocks to warmer cities and even overseas.",
