    "**Q60.** The paragraph below is incomplete. Choose the sentence that completes it most coherently. Yellowstone, founded in 1872, was the world's first national park, created on the then-radical idea that a wilderness could be protected purely for its own sake rather than logged, mined, or farmed for profit. The model spread quickly, and today over one hundred countries maintain some version of a protected national park. Yet parks also draw millions of visitors each year, whose cars, trails, and litter place real strain on the very wilderness the parks exist to protect. ___",
