    "**Q62.** The paragraph below is incomplete. Choose the sentence that completes it most coherently. A steel bridge expands slightly on a hot day and contracts on a cold one, as the metal's molecules vibrate more and take up marginally more space in the heat. Left unaccounted for, this small seasonal expansion could buckle a rigid bridge deck or crack its supports over years of repeated stress. Engineers solve this by inserting expansion joints, gaps filled with flexible material that can widen or narrow as the steel shifts. ___",
