    "**Q88.** The five sentences below, labelled 1 to 5, make a coherent paragraph when properly sequenced. Choose the correct order. 1. What replaced the old metal backing was something more abstract: confidence that a government will keep the currency's supply and value reasonably stable over time. 2. Early paper money in Song-dynasty China worked only because merchants could, in principle, walk into a treasury and exchange the note for a fixed quantity of metal coin. 3. When that confidence collapses, as it periodically has in runaway inflations, the paper notes do not stop existing, but people quietly stop accepting them as payment at all. 4. A modern banknote is, in truth, a promise: a small paper or polymer note that is worth something only because everyone accepts that everyone else will accept it too. 5. Most currencies today have severed that link entirely, and no government promises to hand over gold or silver in exchange for a banknote presented at a counter. *(TITA in the actual exam)*",
    "A) 4-2-5-1-3 B) 4-2-1-5-3 C) 2-4-5-1-3 D) 4-2-5-3-1",
    "<details><summary>Answer & explanation</summary>",
    "",
    "**Correct: A)** Sentence 4 gives the general definition of a banknote as a promise, which is the natural opening. Sentence 2 gives a historical example of that promise being backed by real metal, following the general definition, so 4 is followed by 2. Sentence 5 begins \"Most currencies today have severed that link entirely\" — \"that link\" is the metal-exchange link described in sentence 2, so 2 is followed by 5. Sentence 1 begins \"What replaced the old metal backing\", which only makes sense once sentence 5 has told us the metal backing was severed, so 5 is followed by 1. Sentence 3 begins \"When that confidence collapses\", pointing back to the \"confidence\" introduced in sentence 1, so it comes last. The order is 4-2-5-1-3, option A. Option B swaps sentences 1 and 5, but then sentence 1's \"what replaced the old metal backing\" would appear before we are told the metal backing was actually removed. Option C opens with sentence 2, a specific historical case, before the general definition in sentence 4 has set the stage for it. Option D moves sentence 3 before sentence 1, but \"that confidence\" in sentence 3 has no earlier sentence yet introducing confidence as the new backing.",
    "",
    "📌 *Modeled on: CAT 2025 VARC — para-jumble (TITA) on monetary history, definition-then-example anchor.*",
    "",
    "</details>",
