    "**Q90.** The five sentences below, labelled 1 to 5, make a coherent paragraph when properly sequenced. Choose the correct order. 1. Yet the empathy story cannot be the whole picture, since several species with limited social empathy, including some fish, appear to exhibit contagious yawning of their own. 2. A person only has to see someone else yawn — or even read the word \"yawn\" enough times — to feel the urge rising in their own jaw, a phenomenon called contagious yawning. 3. Some evidence supports the empathy idea directly: children with conditions that affect social bonding tend to catch yawns from others far less often than typically developing children do. 4. The honest conclusion so far is that contagious yawning is probably several overlapping reflexes bundled under one familiar name, not a single, tidy phenomenon with one clean cause. 5. Researchers have long suspected that this contagion has something to do with empathy, since humans catch yawns from people they know far more readily than from strangers. *(TITA in the actual exam)*",
    "A) 2-5-3-1-4 B) 2-3-5-1-4 C) 5-2-3-1-4 D) 2-5-1-3-4",
    "<details><summary>Answer & explanation</summary>",
    "",
    "**Correct: A)** Sentence 2 defines contagious yawning, the natural opening. Sentence 5 begins \"Researchers have long suspected that this contagion...\", where \"this contagion\" points directly back to the phenomenon just defined in sentence 2, so 2 is followed by 5. Sentence 3 begins \"Some evidence supports the empathy idea directly\", and \"the empathy idea\" only exists once sentence 5 has raised the empathy suspicion, so 5 is followed by 3. Sentence 1 begins \"Yet the empathy story cannot be the whole picture\", a contrast that needs the supporting evidence in sentence 3 to already exist before it can be complicated, so 3 is followed by 1. Sentence 4 concludes with the \"honest conclusion so far\", summing up the concede-then-complicate structure just built, so it comes last. The order is 2-5-3-1-4, option A. Option B swaps sentences 3 and 5, but sentence 3's \"the empathy idea\" would then appear before sentence 5 has ever introduced any empathy idea to support. Option C opens with sentence 5, but \"this contagion\" has no earlier sentence defining what the contagion is. Option D moves sentence 1 before sentence 3, but sentence 1's \"yet... cannot be the whole picture\" needs the supporting evidence in sentence 3 to already exist, or there is nothing yet to complicate.",
    "",
    "📌 *Modeled on: CAT 2025 VARC — para-jumble (TITA) on animal-behaviour science, concede-then-complicate anchor.*",
