    "**Q99.** An opening sentence is given, followed by four more sentences labelled 2 to 5. Identify the sentence that does NOT logically belong with the rest of the paragraph. Opening: \"Tea began as a medicinal drink in ancient China long before it became an everyday beverage enjoyed around the world.\" 2. Buddhist monks are said to have valued tea for helping them stay awake during long hours of meditation. 3. Coffee, first cultivated in East Africa, later became the preferred morning drink across much of Europe. 4. Early physicians recommended tea for digestive complaints, alertness, and as a general tonic against fatigue. 5. Only over centuries did tea shift from a medicine cabinet staple to a routine social drink enjoyed for pleasure.",
    "A) Sentence 2 B) Sentence 3 C) Sentence 4 D) Sentence 5",
    "<details><summary>Answer & explanation</summary>",
    "",
    "**Correct: B)** The opening sentence promises a paragraph about tea's own journey from medicine to everyday drink. Sentence 2 stays on topic, giving a specific historical group (monks) who valued tea medicinally. Sentence 4 also stays on topic, giving medical reasons physicians recommended tea. Sentence 5 stays on topic too, describing the shift from medicine to pleasure that the opening sentence promised. Sentence 3, however, suddenly switches subject to coffee's origin and popularity in Europe — a completely different beverage's history, which does not help trace tea's own transition from medicine to daily pleasure at all. Since sentence 3 breaks the paragraph's single throughline about tea, it is the one that does not belong, making B correct.",
