    "**Q100.** An opening sentence is given, followed by four more sentences labelled 2 to 5. Identify the sentence that does NOT logically belong with the rest of the paragraph. Opening: \"Deserts are famous for scorching daytime heat, yet many of the same deserts turn surprisingly cold once the sun sets.\" 2. Deserts are usually defined as regions receiving less than 250 millimetres of rainfall in an average year. 3. Dry desert air contains very little water vapour, and water vapour is what normally traps heat near the ground after sunset. 4. With so little moisture to hold the day's warmth in, desert heat escapes rapidly into the sky once darkness falls. 5. This rapid loss of heat explains why desert nights can feel bitterly cold even after blisteringly hot afternoons.",
    "A) Sentence 2 B) Sentence 3 C) Sentence 4 D) Sentence 5",
    "<details><summary>Answer & explanation</summary>",
    "",
    "**Correct: A)** The opening sentence sets up a specific puzzle to solve: why do hot deserts get cold at night? Sentence 3 starts solving it, explaining that dry air lacks the water vapour that normally traps heat. Sentence 4 continues the chain, explaining that this lack of trapped heat lets warmth escape quickly after sunset. Sentence 5 finishes the chain, stating the conclusion that nights therefore feel cold. Sentence 2, however, only tells us how deserts are officially defined by rainfall amount — a classification fact that does nothing to explain the actual heat-loss mechanism the rest of the paragraph is building, sentence by sentence. Because sentence 2 interrupts this cause-and-effect chain with an unrelated definition, it is the sentence that does not belong, so A is correct.",
