    "**Q101.** An opening sentence is given, followed by four more sentences labelled 2 to 5. Identify the sentence that does NOT logically belong with the rest of the paragraph. Opening: \"Anyone who tries an unfamiliar, intense workout is likely to wake up a day or two later with sore, stiff muscles, a delay that puzzled scientists for a long time.\" 2. The soreness is now understood to come from microscopic tears in muscle fibres, especially after unfamiliar or eccentric movements. 3. The body responds to these tiny tears with local inflammation, which is part of what produces the ache felt over the following days. 4. Repeating the same exercise again soon after seems to produce noticeably less soreness, as the muscle adapts to the specific movement. 5. Regular exercise is recommended by doctors to reduce the risk of heart disease and improve long-term health.",
    "A) Sentence 2 B) Sentence 3 C) Sentence 4 D) Sentence 5",
