    "**Correct: D)** The opening sentence sets up a specific mystery: why does an unfamiliar workout cause delayed muscle soreness? Sentence 2 answers this directly, naming microscopic muscle-fibre tears as the cause. Sentence 3 continues the explanation, describing how inflammation from those tears produces the ache. Sentence 4 adds a further detail about how the soreness lessens on repeating the exercise, staying on the same specific mechanism. Sentence 5, however, jumps to an entirely different and much broader claim about exercise generally reducing heart-disease risk — a general health benefit that has nothing to do with explaining delayed muscle soreness itself. Because it breaks the paragraph's single explanatory thread, sentence 5 does not belong, making D correct.",
