    "**Correct: B)** The opening sentence promises an explanation of how earthworms act like ploughs. Sentence 2 delivers on this, describing how worm tunnels aerate soil. Sentence 4 continues, describing how worm castings enrich soil with nutrients. Sentence 5 wraps up by combining both effects (aeration and enrichment) into a single conclusion about crop yield. Sentence 3, however, switches to home composting, a different household activity that a person chooses to do, which has nothing to do with what earthworms themselves are doing in the soil. Since sentence 3 introduces an unrelated activity rather than continuing the description of earthworm behaviour, it does not belong, making B correct.",
