    "**Q103.** An opening sentence is given, followed by four more sentences labelled 2 to 5. Identify the sentence that does NOT logically belong with the rest of the paragraph. Opening: \"A distant thunderstorm reveals a strange gap: the flash of lightning appears well before its accompanying thunder is heard.\" 2. Light travels fast enough that, across the distance of a typical storm, its arrival is essentially instantaneous. 3. Sound, by contrast, moves through air at only about 340 metres per second, arriving noticeably later over the same distance. 4. Lightning forms when charge builds up between clouds, or between a cloud and the ground, until it discharges suddenly. 5. Counting the seconds between the flash and the thunderclap, then dividing by three, gives a rough distance to the storm in kilometres.",
