    "**Q104.** An opening sentence is given, followed by four more sentences labelled 2 to 5. Identify the sentence that does NOT logically belong with the rest of the paragraph. Opening: \"For more than a century, naturalists have argued over why zebras evolved their distinctive black-and-white stripes.\" 2. Lions, the zebra's main natural predator, are thought to have relatively poor colour vision compared to humans. 3. One leading theory holds that the stripe pattern confuses biting flies, which appear to struggle to land on strongly striped surfaces. 4. Another theory suggests the stripes help zebras recognise individual herd members, since each zebra's pattern is slightly unique. 5. A third theory proposes that stripes help regulate body temperature, since black and white patches may heat unevenly and stir cooling air currents.",
    "A) Sentence 2 B) Sentence 3 C) Sentence 4 D) Sentence 5",
