    "**Correct: A)** The opening sentence promises a list of competing theories for why zebras have stripes. Sentence 3 gives theory one (confusing flies). Sentence 4 gives theory two (herd recognition). Sentence 5 gives theory three (temperature regulation), continuing the same \"one theory... another theory... a third theory\" pattern. Sentence 2, however, gives an isolated fact about lion vision without ever connecting it to any stripe-related theory at all — the paragraph never actually proposes a theory that stripes evade lions, so this fact about lion eyesight just dangles, unconnected to the list. Because it breaks the parallel structure of stated theories, sentence 2 does not belong, making A correct.",
