    "**Q105.** An opening sentence is given, followed by four more sentences labelled 2 to 5. Identify the sentence that does NOT logically belong with the rest of the paragraph. Opening: \"Bread dough left to rest on a kitchen counter slowly swells to nearly double its original size, a transformation driven by living organisms too small to see.\" 2. Yeast cells in the dough consume the sugars present in flour and release carbon dioxide gas as a by-product. 3. Sourdough bread gets its distinctive tang from wild yeast and bacteria rather than from commercially packaged yeast. 4. That gas becomes trapped in thousands of tiny pockets held together by gluten, a stretchy protein network formed when flour is mixed with water. 5. As more pockets fill with gas, the entire mass of dough visibly expands, which is what bakers call the dough \"rising\".",
