    "</details>",
    "",
    "**Q23.** How many more pages did Bhavna read than Chetan?",
    "A) 40 B) 45 C) 50 D) 55",
    "<details><summary>Answer & explanation</summary>",
    "",
    "**Correct: C)** Read both values directly from the table: Bhavna read 175 pages, Chetan read 125 pages. Subtract the smaller from the larger: 175 − 125 = **50**. Option A (40) and option D (55) come from misreading one of the two numbers by a small amount. For a \"how many more\" question, always subtract; never report just one of the two raw numbers.",
    "",
    "📌 *Modeled on: CAT 2025 DILR — direct-lookup difference question inside a reading-habits DI set.*",
    "",
    "</details>",
    "",
    "**Q24.** Esha's pages read is what percentage of the total pages read by all five students?",
    "A) 20% B) 25% C) 30% D) 35%",
    "<details><summary>Answer & explanation</summary>",
    "",
    "**Correct: B)** The total pages read by all five students is 800 (from Q22's working). Esha read 200 pages. The percentage is 200 ÷ 800 × 100. First simplify the fraction: 200 ÷ 800 = 1/4. Then 1/4 as a percentage is **25%**. Option A (20%) and option D (35%) come from using the wrong total in the denominator; option C (30%) comes from a rounding slip. Always find the correct total first, then divide the part by that whole.",
    "",
    "📌 *Modeled on: CAT 2025 DILR — share-of-total percentage question, a common easy DI closer.*",
