    "A) 15 B) 20 C) 25 D) 35",
    "<details><summary>Answer & explanation</summary>",
    "",
    "**Correct: B)** Total coffee drinkers = 40. Of these, 20 also drink tea, so those 20 must be removed to get the coffee-only count. So only-coffee = 40 − 20 = **20**. Option A (15) and option D (35) come from arithmetic slips; option C (25) is not a value produced by this data at all. Always subtract the \"both\" number from the single-sport (or here, single-drink) total, never from the class total.",
