    "[[VIZ]]{\"type\":\"venn2\",\"title\":\"Tea vs coffee drinkers\",\"labels\":[\"Tea\",\"Coffee\"],\"counts\":{\"onlyA\":35,\"onlyB\":20,\"both\":20,\"none\":25}}[[/VIZ]]",
    "",
    "📌 *Modeled on: CAT 2025 DILR — two-set overlap DI, the same easy Venn format seen across multiple slots.*",
    "",
    "</details>",
    "",
    "**Q34.** How many employees drink neither tea nor coffee?",
    "A) 20 B) 25 C) 30 D) 35",
    "<details><summary>Answer & explanation</summary>",
    "",
    "**Correct: B)** Only-tea = 55 − 20 = 35. Only-coffee = 40 − 20 = 20 (from Q33). Both = 20. Add the three non-overlapping groups: 35 + 20 + 20 = 75 employees drink at least one of the two. Out of 100 total employees, the number drinking neither is 100 − 75 = **25**. Option A (20) mistakes the \"both\" count for the \"neither\" count; option D (35) mistakes the only-tea count for it. Build the at-least-one total first, then subtract from the grand total.",
    "",
    "📌 *Modeled on: CAT 2025 DILR — complement (neither) question inside a two-set overlap scenario.*",
    "",
    "</details>",
