    "**Q35.** How many employees drink at least one of the two beverages?",
    "A) 65 B) 70 C) 75 D) 95",
    "<details><summary>Answer & explanation</summary>",
    "",
    "**Correct: C)** Use the direct union rule: tea + coffee − both = 55 + 40 − 20. First add 55 + 40 = 95. Then subtract the 20 who were counted twice (once in tea, once in coffee): 95 − 20 = **75**. This matches the sum of only-tea (35), only-coffee (20) and both (20) from Q34: 35 + 20 + 20 = 75. Option D (95) forgets to remove the double-counted \"both\" group entirely.",
    "",
    "📌 *Modeled on: CAT 2025 DILR — union-of-two-sets question, testing the standard overlap subtraction rule.*",
