    "",
    "**Correct: B)** \"Exactly one\" means only-tea plus only-coffee, excluding anyone who drinks both. From Q33–Q34: only-tea = 35, only-coffee = 20. Add these: 35 + 20 = **55**. Option D (75) is the at-least-one total from Q35, which wrongly includes the 20 who drink both; option C (65) comes from adding only one of the only-groups to the both-group by mistake. \"Exactly one\" always means add the two only-groups and stop.",
    "",
    "📌 *Modeled on: CAT 2025 DILR — exactly-one-of-two-sets question, a recurring easy Venn-diagram type.*",
    "",
    "</details>",
